+# Fix lower-case SKU lookup, delivery threshold, and VAT rounding
+
+Three reports this week against the order service. Each is a departure from the business rules in
+`README.md`, which is the reference.
+
+1. **Lower-case SKU refused (sales desk, Giulia).** Keying a product code in lower case, as customers
+   read it out (`lb-220`), is refused as an unknown product; the same code in capitals works. The README
+   says SKUs are case-insensitive and always shown in upper case.
+   - Fix: `Catalog.find` must canonicalise the SKU (trim and upper-case), as `Catalog.add` already does.
+
+2. **Delivery charged at €50.00 (customer, Marco).** A basket of €50.00 after discount was charged €4.90
+   for delivery. The README says shipping is free when the goods come to €50.00 **or more**.
+   - Fix: `shippingCost` must treat goods of exactly 5000 cents as free (`>=`, not `>`).
+
+3. **VAT one cent low on some lines (accounting).** A single item at €1.99 at the standard rate shows
+   €0.43 of VAT on its line; the correct figure is €0.44. The README says VAT is rounded half up to the
+   cent on each line.
+   - Fix: `lineVat` must round half up (through `percentOf`), not truncate.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- A lower-case or padded SKU orders and quotes the same as its upper-case form.
+- Goods of exactly €50.00 after discount ship free; €49.99 still pays the band cost.
+- A €1.99 line at the standard rate carries €0.44 of VAT.
+- The existing test suite still passes; new tests cover each of the three cases.
